  "reason": "The occurrence 'motor neurons supplying opposing extensor muscles' describes a specific subset of motor neurons (those controlling extensors that oppose flexors). The existing concept 'motor neurons supplying flexor muscles' refers to the distinct set of motor neurons controlling flexors. While they are functionally linked via reciprocal inhibition in spinal reflexes, they represent different biological entities with different targets and functions. Therefore, they are not aliases but related concepts at the same level of specificity."
